@anon.a2b023d1a4e2834952d16152dce23780.917 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [1375 x i8] }> <{ [1375 x i8] c"Extracts the components of this color.\0A\0AThe size and values of this array depends on the color space. You can\0Aobtain the color space using [`space`]($color.space). Below is a table\0Aof the color spaces and their components:\0A\0A|       Color space       |     C1    |     C2     |     C3    |   C4   |\0A|-------------------------|-----------|------------|-----------|--------|\0A| [`luma`]($color.luma)   | Lightness |            |           |        |\0A| [`oklab`]($color.oklab) | Lightness |    `a`     |    `b`    |  Alpha |\0A| [`oklch`]($color.oklch) | Lightness |   Chroma   |    Hue    |  Alpha |\0A| [`linear-rgb`]($color.linear-rgb) | Red  |   Green |    Blue |  Alpha |\0A| [`rgb`]($color.rgb)     |    Red    |   Green    |    Blue   |  Alpha |\0A| [`cmyk`]($color.cmyk)   |    Cyan   |   Magenta  |   Yellow  |  Key   |\0A| [`hsl`]($color.hsl)     |     Hue   | Saturation | Lightness |  Alpha |\0A| [`hsv`]($color.hsv)     |     Hue   | Saturation |   Value   |  Alpha |\0A\0AFor the meaning and type of each individual value, see the documentation\0Aof the corresponding color space. The alpha component is optional and\0Aonly included if the `alpha` argument is `true`. The length of the\0Areturned array depends on the number of components and whether the alpha\0Acomponent is included.\0A\0A```example\0A// note that the alpha component is included by default\0A#rgb(40%, 60%, 80%).components()\0A```" }>, align 1
